News - How To Drill For Water According To The Terrain
For the average well driller, the drilling of a water well drilling rig is nothing more than to quickly find the drilling position of a large amount of water. If there is insufficient experience, it is likely that the well will be drilled without water.
“There is a ditch between two mountains, and there is water flow in the ditch rock.” There is a valley between the two mountains, and it is easy to find water sources in the rock layers on both banks of the lower reaches of the river valley.
“The two ditches intersect and the spring water rushes.” There may be spring water beneath the mountain mouth where the two ditches meet. If you dig a well here, the water source is more reliable.
“Shanzui vs. Shanzui, there is good water under the mouth”. The two shanks are opposite and close to each other.
“Two mountains and a lone mountain are often dry.” If the rock layer under the Gushan becomes a water-proof layer due to the local variation of lithology, it can block the flow of groundwater, and by drilling a well upstream of the Gushan, the water can be discharged.
“Mountains are low, and the amount of spring water is large when digging wells.” The mountains are connected so far that they are submerged, and groundwater can be found in the aquifer where the topography of the submerged end is appropriate.
“The mountain turns its head and there is water”. The low area of the mountain bay caused by the twisting of the mountain blocks the groundwater flowing down the mountain, enriching in the aquifer, and there is water in the well.
“Convex mountain to concave mountain, good water is in the concave room”. The shape of one mountain is convex toward the opposite side, and the shape of the other mountain is concave inward.
“The big mountain bursts out of a spout, and there is much water in the well.” A shorter mountain protrudes in the middle of the Changshan Mountain. Drilling wells in the lower part of the slope of this mountain Tsui generally produces water.
Look for ancient river channels along the river. Although the ancient river channel is now buried, the aquifer is gravel, and there is still diving flow, which is a good place to drill wells.
