1. The number of working procedures of precision stamping parts mainly depends on the complexity of its structure shape and depends on the number of bending angles, relative positions and bending directions.When the bending radius of the bending part is less than the allowable value, a shaping procedure is added after bending.
The number of working procedures of precision stamping parts is related to material properties, drawing height, number of drawing steps, drawing diameter and material thickness, etc., which can only be determined by drawing process calculation.When the rounded corner radius of drawing part is small or the dimensional precision is high, it is necessary to add a shaping procedure after drawing.
The determination of the number of processes shall also be in line with the existing molding capacity and stamping equipment of the enterprise.Mold making capacity should be able to ensure that the mold processing, assembly accuracy corresponding to the requirements of improvement, otherwise only to increase the number of procedures.
When the section quality and dimensional accuracy of precision stamping parts are required to be higher, it can be considered to add dressing procedure after blanking or directly adopt the precision blanking procedure.
