The bag filter is composed of a suction pipe, a dust collector body, a filtering device, a blowing device and a suction and exhaust device. Below we explain the composition and function of each part.
Dust suction pipe: The dust suction pipe is the key to adjust the air volume and pressure of each dust suction port. This requires data calculation and selection of suitable size pipes according to the working conditions.
Clean air chamber: It is the space to isolate the smoke and dust and clean the bag dust, so its airtightness must be good to ensure that the filtered gas meets the emission standards.
Dust removal frame: It is the support for the dust removal bag. Only if it has sufficient strength can the dust collector bag not be sucked and ensure the normal operation of the dust collector.
Blow pipe: It is a device to ensure that the gas sprayed by the electromagnetic pulse valve is evenly distributed to the mouth of each cloth bag.
Chimney: a qualified gas discharge device, which is generally larger than the main pipe of the smoke and dust inlet to ensure smooth discharge.
