The only way to deal with wind, humidity and cold temperatures when cooking outdoors is with a high-pressure propane burner. High-pressure burners work simply: a high-pressure regulator lets more propane reach the burner, which turns it into a hotter flame.
If you live in an area that doesn't have access to a natural-gas pipeline network and prefer gas, a low-pressure propane stove is your best option. Hotels, restaurants and resorts on islands and in mountainous regions commonly use propane in their kitchens.
