Step 2: Lecture, demonstration, and practice using BMI Table
Find the person’s weight in the top row.
Imagine another straight line that runs from Top to Bottom from the person’s weight.
If the two lines meet between two numbers, the BMI is the lower number plus 0.5 (for example, between 19 and 20, the BMI is 19.5). If the lines meet between two of the same numbers, that is the BMI.
The Body Mass Index (BMI) is not used to monitor weight in pregnancy because the body weight will change due to the growing baby in utero/fetus.
